{"name":"Larimar Blue","hex":"#1d78ab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"larimar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rare blue variety of pectolite found only in the Dominican Republic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/larimar"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Larimar","blocks":[{"text":"Larimar is the tradename for a rare blue variety of the silicate mineral pectolite found only in the Dominican Republic, around the city of Barahona. Its coloration varies from bluish white, light-blue, light-green, teal, green-blue, turquoise blue, turquoise green, turquoise blue-green, deep green, dark green, to deep blue, dark blue and purple, violet and indigo and the larimar can come in many varieties and color mixes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Larimar.jpg/330px-Larimar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larimar","wikidata":"Q2502146"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Larimar_1%28R%C3%A9publique_Dominicaine%29.jpg/500px-Larimar_1%28R%C3%A9publique_Dominicaine%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Larimar_1%28R%C3%A9publique_Dominicaine%29.jpg/1280px-Larimar_1%28R%C3%A9publique_Dominicaine%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Larimar_1%28R%C3%A9publique_Dominicaine%29.jpg/500px-Larimar_1%28R%C3%A9publique_Dominicaine%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rough Larimar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALarimar_1(R%C3%A9publique_Dominicaine).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BB_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_010.jpg/500px-2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BB_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BB_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_010.jpg/1280px-2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%